   132	their procedural alternatives; instead, comprehensions make change
   133	tasks worse than their procedural alternatives; (ii) procedural code
   134	is generally perceived as more readable than its functional alternative; and (iii) developers found functional constructs useful to
   135	shorten the source code, even if they are challenging to debug.
   136	Results of the study provide empirical evidence on the difficulties
   137	experienced by developers when using functional constructs, also
