   221	**List Comprehensions.** A list comprehension iterates over a list
   222	of objects, checks for a specified condition (if any), and computes an
   223	expression. This computed value becomes an element in the newly
   224	created collection (as shown in Listing 2). A list comprehension can
   225	be defined with the following syntax:
   226	
   227	[expression **for** item **in** iterable **if** condition]
   228	**Map/Reduce/Filter Functions.** Map(), reduce() and filter(),
   229	are three high-order Python functions. They take a function as a
   230	parameter and return a function. They have a similar syntax:
   231	FUN (function, iterable)
